sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/hollow-tube-mass-optimality--claude-opus-5-5--2> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-taxon test of K against marrow-adjusted optimum and buckling limit" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/hollow-tube-mass-optimality> ;
    dct:description "Compile at least 100 structures from four types: marrow-filled mammal long bones, pneumatic and marrow-filled bird long bones, bamboo culms and hollow grass stems, and feather rachises, each with outer radius, wall thickness and tissue modulus from the same or a matched source. For each, compute three predictions from approach 1: K*(q) (core-mass-adjusted stiffness optimum), K_b (Brazier local-buckling limit using measured E and an assumed strength-to-modulus ratio stated per tissue) and the predicted value min(K*, K_b). The sharpest test is within birds: pneumatic bones carry no marrow mass, so they are predicted to sit nearer K_b, while marrow-filled bones of the same birds should sit near K*(q). Classify each structure as at-optimum (|K - K*| <= 0.05), at-buckling (|K - K_b| <= 0.05), or neither; test size dependence by regressing K on log body or structure mass with phylogenetic GLS for the animal subset." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Proportions of structures at K*, at K_b and at neither, with the pneumatic-versus-filled contrast in birds; Thompson's optimality claim is supported if most filled structures fall within 0.05 of K* and pneumatic ones are shifted toward K_b." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Most structures fall in the 'neither' class, or the pneumatic-filled contrast is absent or reversed; or fewer than 100 structures have a matched modulus, in which case the test is underpowered rather than decisive." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/data-test" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Pre-register the tolerance (0.05 in K), the q values per tissue, and the classification rule. 2. Extract K and E from Currey and Alexander 1985 and other primary tables found by a pre-registered search; resolve taxa through the organisms layer (GBIF, NCBI). 3. Compute predictions and classify; run the paired pneumatic-versus-marrow comparison with a sign test and a mixed model with species as random effect. 4. Fit K versus log mass, phylogenetically corrected for vertebrates." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Matched tissue moduli for feather rachises and many plant stems are sparse; bird pneumaticity status per bone must be extracted from anatomical literature." ;
    skos:note "Tool: literature-extraction" ;
    skos:note "Tool: organisms-layer" ;
    skos:note "Tool: gbif" ;
    skos:note "Tool: r-phylolm" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-03> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-04> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7998.1985.tb03551.x> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1995.0075> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1995.0076> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/hollow-tube-mass-optimality> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Are biological hollow structures at the stiffness-per-mass optimum?" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7998.1985.tb03551.x> dct:title "The thickness of the walls of tubular bones" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Currey and Alexander 1985, The thickness of the walls of tubular bones" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1995.0075> dct:title "The mechanical properties of natural materials. I. Material property charts" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Ashby, Gibson, Wegst and Olive 1995, Material property charts" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1995.0076> dct:title "The mechanical properties of natural materials. II. Microstructures for mechanical efficiency" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Gibson, Ashby, Wegst and Olive 1995, Microstructures for mechanical efficiency" .
}

